WEBVTT

00:43.460 --> 00:48.465
DOONA!

00:50.884 --> 00:51.968
"I'm glad."

00:53.553 --> 00:54.721
"I'm glad."

00:57.307 --> 00:58.600
"I'm glad."

00:58.641 --> 00:59.726
EPISODE 3
SPRING BREEZE

00:59.768 --> 01:03.229
What do you think that means?
From a girl's point of view.

01:05.273 --> 01:07.400
It could mean two things.

01:09.736 --> 01:10.653
Number one!

01:11.905 --> 01:13.948
"I'm glad that you, whom I like,

01:14.032 --> 01:17.368
have nothing going on with her."

01:19.537 --> 01:21.164
Number two! "Doona?"

01:22.832 --> 01:24.417
"I'm not keen on her."

01:25.168 --> 01:27.045
"Well, I'm glad you're not with her."

01:28.296 --> 01:29.672
I don't think it's either.

01:30.882 --> 01:32.717
God, are you stupid?

01:32.801 --> 01:34.052
It's obviously number one.

01:34.677 --> 01:36.596
Why would Jin-ju like me?

01:39.432 --> 01:40.391
Why not?

01:41.351 --> 01:42.769
I like you.

01:45.396 --> 01:46.981
You're smiling.

01:48.775 --> 01:51.444
I'm not saying
there's anything wrong with me.

01:52.028 --> 01:52.904
It's just…

01:53.905 --> 01:55.240
It's difficult with Jin-ju.

01:57.450 --> 01:59.536
You think too much.

02:00.870 --> 02:02.288
Just live a bit in the present.

02:03.123 --> 02:06.668
True feelings that can be felt
without words? They don't exist.

02:08.378 --> 02:11.172
Well, if you get hurt,
I can at least be a shoulder to cry on.

02:11.673 --> 02:13.466
Isn't that what friends are for?

02:41.035 --> 02:43.580
FOR SOPHOMORES
THE ART OF MATHEMATICS

03:02.223 --> 03:03.433
Won-jun, come quick.

03:03.933 --> 03:05.351
- Close that.
- Okay.

03:05.852 --> 03:08.646
Five, four, three,

03:08.730 --> 03:10.440
two, one.

03:14.694 --> 03:17.322
Five, four, three,

03:17.405 --> 03:19.449
two, one.

03:22.827 --> 03:25.496
Five, four, three,

03:26.080 --> 03:27.999
two, one.

03:29.918 --> 03:31.044
Seriously?

03:31.127 --> 03:33.171
If you're going to do it, do it right.

03:33.254 --> 03:35.465
- Here, like this.
- Five.

03:36.049 --> 03:39.719
Four, three, two, one.

03:54.192 --> 03:57.862
There's a rumor going around
that we're together.

03:58.446 --> 04:00.156
- I know.
- But it's not true.

04:00.740 --> 04:02.408
We're just close, right?

04:03.660 --> 04:05.078
What do you say

04:05.161 --> 04:08.122
when people ask you
what the deal is between us?

04:08.998 --> 04:09.874
What about you?

04:10.750 --> 04:12.043
What do you say?

04:12.126 --> 04:14.629
Well,

04:16.089 --> 04:17.215
just that we're close.

04:19.008 --> 04:20.301
That we get on well.

04:23.263 --> 04:24.931
That we're like soulmates.

04:30.603 --> 04:31.604
That's so true.

04:32.522 --> 04:34.482
I like that! Soulmates.

04:48.413 --> 04:49.622
This one looks good.

04:50.873 --> 04:51.708
Only you do.

04:53.251 --> 04:55.003
You look good in it too!

06:04.030 --> 06:06.491
Happy birthday. I'll be in touch.

07:37.498 --> 07:39.041
I'm sorry for the delay.

07:39.125 --> 07:41.085
We're really backed up with orders.

07:41.169 --> 07:42.295
Please enjoy.

08:06.736 --> 08:09.071
I'm so sorry.
I spilled some coffee over there.

08:10.573 --> 08:11.491
I'll get it.

08:11.574 --> 08:13.701
- Okay. Thank you.
- No problem.

08:25.838 --> 08:26.923
Jin-ju.

08:28.341 --> 08:29.175
Yeah?

08:30.176 --> 08:31.719
What are you doing tomorrow?

08:32.678 --> 08:34.138
Tomorrow…

08:34.805 --> 08:37.266
Want to go see the cherry blossoms?
If you're busy--

08:37.350 --> 08:38.226
No! I…

08:41.771 --> 08:42.772
Sure!

08:44.524 --> 08:45.525
Okay.

09:42.915 --> 09:44.584
Doona, where are you?

09:47.878 --> 09:49.213
Are you sleeping?

09:53.342 --> 09:54.468
Doona!

09:58.889 --> 10:00.057
Doona!

10:03.728 --> 10:05.521
Doona, are you in there?

10:06.022 --> 10:07.148
I'm trapped.

10:09.108 --> 10:12.320
- Can you open it for me?
- Hang in there for just a sec!

11:22.390 --> 11:24.016
A penny for your thoughts.

11:27.228 --> 11:28.104
So hot.

11:29.522 --> 11:32.316
A man who fixes bathroom doors is so hot.

11:32.400 --> 11:35.194
My god. You're unbelievable.

11:37.363 --> 11:38.322
I'm serious.

11:39.782 --> 11:41.867
Maybe it's because I don't have a dad,

11:42.618 --> 11:44.578
but it's kind of like a fantasy of mine.

11:46.163 --> 11:47.331
Your father isn't around?

11:47.998 --> 11:48.833
No.

11:48.916 --> 11:50.751
My father died when I was young too.

11:55.089 --> 11:56.465
I never had one to start with.

11:57.967 --> 12:00.177
Life must have been hard for you too.

12:00.261 --> 12:01.262
Not really.

12:02.930 --> 12:04.515
It's actually convenient

12:04.598 --> 12:08.561
since I can imagine my father
to be whatever I want.

12:10.438 --> 12:12.189
Do you know what's really hard?

12:12.982 --> 12:15.151
It's not someone who was never there.

12:15.735 --> 12:18.529
It's people who disappear on you
when they were there before.

12:19.029 --> 12:20.823
That's what drives you insane.

12:25.953 --> 12:26.954
That's right.

12:27.037 --> 12:28.789
These had disappeared on me too.

12:31.375 --> 12:35.671
Oh, I think I saw a pack in the cabinet
while I was looking for the toolbox.

12:37.673 --> 12:38.507
That one?

12:51.687 --> 12:52.938
These aren't mine.

12:55.107 --> 12:57.359
Why would I smoke something like that?

12:58.319 --> 12:59.195
Hey…

13:01.197 --> 13:02.281
shall we go out?

13:04.325 --> 13:07.870
There seem to be a lot of people's heads
you want to smash. So let's do it.

13:09.747 --> 13:10.831
Give it a go.

13:11.791 --> 13:12.625
Here.

13:22.510 --> 13:23.344
Faster!

13:23.427 --> 13:24.929
Whack them hard to score points.

13:25.012 --> 13:26.722
Think of all the people you hate.

13:26.806 --> 13:27.640
Faster!

13:28.599 --> 13:30.309
Neener, neener! Getting angry?

13:34.104 --> 13:35.648
There's a pattern to this.

13:36.148 --> 13:38.275
That hurts!

13:38.359 --> 13:40.069
Don't hit me!

13:40.152 --> 13:41.153
You're good.

13:41.779 --> 13:43.322
That hurts!

13:43.405 --> 13:45.991
It's fun, right? Oh, there's one.

13:46.075 --> 13:47.952
Here. There.

13:48.536 --> 13:49.370
That hurts!

13:50.246 --> 13:51.080
Great job!

13:52.206 --> 13:54.083
- Nice.
- I want to go again.

13:55.918 --> 13:56.752
Go for it.

13:57.378 --> 13:59.088
That hurts!

14:01.215 --> 14:02.049
That's it.

14:02.132 --> 14:03.050
Don't hit me!

14:04.510 --> 14:05.511
That hurts!

14:05.594 --> 14:07.179
YOUR SCORE

14:13.644 --> 14:15.980
That hurts!

14:24.238 --> 14:25.573
How did that not go in?

14:37.960 --> 14:39.169
Come on, go in!

14:43.883 --> 14:45.676
Give me the ball!

15:10.409 --> 15:11.785
- Nice.
- I'm beat!

15:17.541 --> 15:18.375
Hey!

15:20.294 --> 15:21.670
You should lie down too.

15:23.839 --> 15:24.965
It's really pretty.

15:39.146 --> 15:40.522
Why are you laughing?

15:41.440 --> 15:44.735
What are you calling pretty?
I can't see a single star.

15:45.319 --> 15:47.321
It's really overcast at the moment.

15:48.656 --> 15:51.700
- It looks like it will rain tomorrow.
- Do you think?

15:55.245 --> 15:56.455
It looked pretty

15:57.831 --> 15:58.832
regardless.

16:05.422 --> 16:07.007
Thanks for today.

16:08.801 --> 16:10.052
For everything.

16:10.636 --> 16:11.595
You too.

16:12.471 --> 16:15.849
I can't remember the last time
I let go like this and had fun.

16:22.356 --> 16:24.483
I asked Jin-ju to go see
the cherry blossoms with me.

16:26.944 --> 16:27.778
Really?

16:27.861 --> 16:28.821
Did she say yes?

16:31.740 --> 16:35.494
I thought she'd say no, but yeah.
I'm not sure why.

16:37.162 --> 16:38.372
Don't run away.

16:38.998 --> 16:40.124
It can become a habit.

16:42.710 --> 16:44.128
I won't.

17:26.628 --> 17:28.630
The weather…

17:29.381 --> 17:30.466
"Clear and sunny."

17:53.280 --> 17:54.448
Won-jun!

17:59.912 --> 18:01.705
They're so pretty!

18:01.789 --> 18:04.333
They are, aren't they?
Wow, there are so many of them.

18:04.416 --> 18:05.250
Yeah.

18:06.126 --> 18:09.588
Oh, right. Kook Su-jin's apartment complex
has really pretty cherry blossoms.

18:10.172 --> 18:11.340
Do you remember?

18:11.423 --> 18:13.342
Yes. That's right.

18:13.425 --> 18:16.762
Didn't we skip a day of academy classes
to hang out in that playground?

18:17.846 --> 18:20.265
Skip a day? Are you kidding me?

18:20.349 --> 18:22.893
You were determined
not to miss the revision class,

18:22.976 --> 18:24.812
so we run back after just 20 minutes.

18:26.730 --> 18:31.985
Lee Won-jun was never even late for class,
let alone skipping one.

18:32.569 --> 18:33.862
You're really something.

18:44.540 --> 18:46.083
- Oh, the other day--
- The other--

18:47.000 --> 18:49.795
- You go first.
- No, you go first.

18:50.921 --> 18:53.423
I came across a whack-a-mole
in my neighborhood.

18:53.507 --> 18:55.843
The one you were obsessed with
outside the academy?

18:55.926 --> 18:56.885
Really?

18:57.636 --> 19:00.931
I've been really missing it.
I haven't been able to play it in Seoul.

19:01.014 --> 19:02.307
Have you?

19:02.808 --> 19:04.685
No, not me. Only Doona has.

19:05.769 --> 19:07.062
It was her first time.

19:07.146 --> 19:09.189
Everything she does seems to be her first.

19:14.319 --> 19:15.612
What were you going to say?

19:15.696 --> 19:16.697
I don't know.

19:18.282 --> 19:19.283
I can't remember.

19:27.541 --> 19:28.750
It's raining.

19:58.238 --> 19:59.072
Jin-ju.

20:11.793 --> 20:13.879
- Here.
- Thank you.

20:13.962 --> 20:16.298
- Get under this. It's cold.
- Oh, thank you.

20:24.890 --> 20:26.725
YUN-TAEK

20:26.767 --> 20:29.519
- May I take this call?
- Of course, please go ahead.

20:31.188 --> 20:32.564
Yes, Yun-taek?

20:32.648 --> 20:34.858
Won-jun, when are you back?
We ordered pizza.

20:34.942 --> 20:36.693
It was two-for-one, so we got four.

20:37.486 --> 20:40.280
Is that Seo Yun-taek
you're talking to on the phone?

20:41.240 --> 20:43.992
Yes. Do you know him?

20:44.576 --> 20:47.162
Wow! What a small world.

20:47.663 --> 20:49.790
Won-jun's friend from back home

20:49.873 --> 20:52.251
and my best friend are connected like…

20:52.751 --> 20:54.044
Like this. Right?

20:55.837 --> 20:57.798
Jin-ju, what can I say about Se-hun?

20:58.298 --> 21:01.760
Call me biased,
but he really is an impressive bastard.

21:02.344 --> 21:04.721
First of all, he's tall.
He's good-looking.

21:05.889 --> 21:06.723
He's also rich.

21:06.807 --> 21:09.601
Oh, and he's freaking amazing at sports.

21:09.685 --> 21:11.478
So his body's ripped!

21:11.561 --> 21:14.398
His legs are like,
you know what I mean, right?

21:14.481 --> 21:16.358
- You've lucked out.
- Cut it out, man.

21:16.441 --> 21:18.610
He's like that when he's drunk.
Just ignore him.

21:18.694 --> 21:19.903
It's okay.

21:22.990 --> 21:23.824
So?

21:24.491 --> 21:25.867
Are you two an item, then?

21:26.493 --> 21:28.120
No, it's nothing like that--

21:28.203 --> 21:29.538
We're like soulmates.

21:30.122 --> 21:31.873
Because we get on so well.

21:33.333 --> 21:34.167
Yeah.

21:36.253 --> 21:39.631
You should date!

21:39.715 --> 21:41.174
- Kiss!
- Yun-taek.

21:41.883 --> 21:44.261
You should have some food.

21:44.344 --> 21:46.513
You must be hungry from talking so much.

21:46.596 --> 21:48.682
Ms. Lee,

21:49.308 --> 21:54.062
did you just call me by my name?
Have I finally become visible to you?

21:54.146 --> 21:56.940
Where's the tranquilizer gun?
Why are you so chatty today?

21:57.024 --> 21:58.734
Am I talking too much?

21:59.234 --> 22:00.610
You can talk too, you know?

22:00.694 --> 22:02.321
I've become visible to her.

22:02.404 --> 22:03.697
I've finally become visible…

22:03.780 --> 22:05.490
I'll go buy some ice cream for us.

22:06.199 --> 22:07.034
All right.

22:09.536 --> 22:10.537
Cheers!

22:11.705 --> 22:14.166
You know,
when we were doing national service…

22:42.944 --> 22:43.945
You came.

22:44.029 --> 22:45.989
My soulmate.

22:53.705 --> 22:55.957
It looks like
I'm going to have to resit my exams.

22:57.626 --> 23:00.879
I wanted to go to the same college as you,
but it's not going to happen.

23:04.883 --> 23:05.967
It's cold.

23:34.454 --> 23:35.831
Is that better?

23:42.921 --> 23:43.922
No.

23:45.549 --> 23:46.842
I'm still cold.

24:17.330 --> 24:19.499
You have surprisingly old-fashioned taste.

24:19.583 --> 24:21.376
You like toe socks too.

24:22.461 --> 24:23.753
Aren't you cold?

24:23.837 --> 24:25.964
Not at all! I'm immune to the cold.

24:33.221 --> 24:34.222
These are different.

24:35.348 --> 24:37.767
- What are?
- The cherry blossoms.

24:37.851 --> 24:40.896
Yangjin and Seoul have different ones,
and these are different too.

24:44.524 --> 24:46.067
Should I tell you why?

24:46.610 --> 24:47.569
Do you know why?

24:49.321 --> 24:53.200
Those are apricot blossoms,
not cherry blossoms, you dummy.

24:53.283 --> 24:56.286
Oh, really?
How do you know something like that?

24:56.786 --> 24:58.705
I'm more knowledgeable than you.

24:59.206 --> 25:01.124
So you should treat me as your teacher.

25:01.666 --> 25:02.626
Yes, Ms. Lee.

25:03.210 --> 25:04.669
You go ahead and go in.

25:05.545 --> 25:07.589
- What about you?
- I'm going to have a smoke.

25:09.382 --> 25:13.220
- Do you want me to keep you company?
- No, the ice cream will melt.

25:14.137 --> 25:15.972
- Can you throw this away for me?
- Sure.

25:17.474 --> 25:18.350
All right, then.

25:34.699 --> 25:37.786
- Here we are. Ice cream.
- Ice cream!

25:38.912 --> 25:39.996
Thank you.

25:40.622 --> 25:41.456
Here you go.

25:42.707 --> 25:45.418
- Here's your favorite.
- Oh! Thank you.

25:45.919 --> 25:48.004
Hey, Doona. Hurry over
and have your ice cream.

25:49.798 --> 25:52.968
- What were you talking about?
- Oh, yes.

25:53.051 --> 25:54.344
Right, so,

25:55.178 --> 25:57.639
the wild boar is charging toward me.

25:57.722 --> 25:59.558
Wild boars are really fast, you know?

25:59.641 --> 26:02.477
I obviously couldn't outrun it.

26:02.561 --> 26:04.437
So I thought, "Let's jump on its back!"

26:05.480 --> 26:08.858
I took a jump and landed on its back,
except I was facing backward.

26:08.942 --> 26:12.404
So I'm riding it backward like clip, clop,
and all hell is breaking loose.

26:12.487 --> 26:14.864
People are shouting,
"Yun-taek, where are you going?"

26:14.948 --> 26:17.409
"I'll return on boar-back, sir!"

26:17.492 --> 26:20.495
- And I grabbed its tail to steer it.
- Stop lying, man.

26:20.579 --> 26:24.541
Of course it's a lie, jackass.
How could this possibly be true? God…

26:25.750 --> 26:26.793
You're really drunk.

26:27.294 --> 26:30.046
- So, what? Just flirting?
- So far, yes.

26:31.548 --> 26:34.009
- Jin-ju's cute, isn't she?
- What?

26:37.512 --> 26:38.430
Jeez!

26:39.389 --> 26:41.433
Anyhow, congratulations, man.

26:49.232 --> 26:50.900
Doona, can I come hang out again?

26:53.069 --> 26:54.195
You can come every day.

27:00.035 --> 27:02.662
- Come on, let's go, everyone!
- Mark him!

27:05.206 --> 27:08.543
Come on, let's go, Korean Lit!

27:08.627 --> 27:11.004
- Okay, let's go!
- Mark him!

27:11.087 --> 27:12.547
- It's open!
- Over here!

27:12.631 --> 27:14.674
- It's open!
- Won-jun, it's open!

27:18.762 --> 27:21.097
- They're going to end up fighting.
- No way.

27:21.181 --> 27:23.558
Won-jun would never.
He'd rather give up the ball.

27:31.024 --> 27:32.817
Nice!

27:33.735 --> 27:36.404
Don't worry about it! It's all right!

27:36.488 --> 27:37.864
- Good job!
- Yay!

27:38.573 --> 27:40.158
- Let's go, Korean Lit!
- Time out.

27:40.241 --> 27:41.409
KOR LIT
CIV ENG

27:43.078 --> 27:45.413
- What's going on?
- Hold onto this for me.

27:45.997 --> 27:46.831
Sure.

27:48.124 --> 27:48.958
Let's go!

27:49.876 --> 27:52.462
- Come on, Se-hun!
- Jeong!

27:52.545 --> 27:55.548
Korean Lit!

27:55.632 --> 27:57.300
- Finish it off!
- Block it!

27:57.384 --> 27:59.302
- Nice!
- Okay!

28:02.180 --> 28:03.014
Nice!

28:03.515 --> 28:05.600
Come on, guys! Let's go!

28:05.684 --> 28:06.601
We've got this!

28:07.602 --> 28:09.020
Come on, Korean Lit!

28:09.604 --> 28:11.272
Come on! Let's go!

28:11.356 --> 28:12.357
Good job!

28:12.440 --> 28:14.025
- Well played.
- Good job.

28:14.109 --> 28:15.151
Hey, good job.

28:18.530 --> 28:20.240
- Good job.
- Thanks.

28:23.159 --> 28:25.036
Jin-ju, you're coming for lunch, right?

28:26.579 --> 28:29.082
There's a new pasta place
just across the street.

28:29.165 --> 28:30.291
Let's all go together.

28:31.876 --> 28:33.461
I have a class now.

28:35.380 --> 28:36.631
Just us, then?

28:38.466 --> 28:39.300
Okay!

28:40.260 --> 28:42.011
- Let's do this again sometime.
- Sure.

28:45.056 --> 28:46.015
I'll see you later.

28:46.641 --> 28:47.475
Let's go.

29:08.496 --> 29:10.457
Did you miss class because of me?

29:10.540 --> 29:12.500
I didn't want to go anyway.

29:15.295 --> 29:18.381
You'll lose her if you keep on like that.
Are you okay with that?

29:18.882 --> 29:20.675
How can I lose her, Ms. Lee?

29:20.759 --> 29:21.968
She's not mine to lose.

29:22.051 --> 29:23.636
That's not true.

29:23.720 --> 29:27.098
From where I'm standing, you and Jin-ju
feel the same way about each other

29:27.182 --> 29:28.600
but are just being stupid.

29:29.184 --> 29:31.352
At least make a go of it before giving up.

29:31.436 --> 29:33.146
I'm frustrated just looking at you.

29:34.856 --> 29:35.899
I have.

29:36.900 --> 29:39.110
I told her I had feelings for her.

29:39.194 --> 29:40.236
I did.

29:42.280 --> 29:43.114
You did?

29:43.198 --> 29:44.449
Yes.

29:44.949 --> 29:46.910
I thought she felt the same way.

29:57.295 --> 29:58.296
I like you.

30:18.191 --> 30:20.485
The number you're trying to reach
is currently…

30:20.568 --> 30:22.028
Is everything okay?

30:25.323 --> 30:29.118
Sorry, I've been busy.
I'll contact you later.

30:33.873 --> 30:34.791
MAYBE

30:36.626 --> 30:39.921
COULD WE

30:46.386 --> 30:50.223
COULD YOU COME OUT FOR

30:52.892 --> 30:54.602
This could feed two dozen people.

30:54.686 --> 30:56.229
We can easily finish this.

30:56.312 --> 30:58.064
Of course we can eat it all!

31:09.784 --> 31:10.785
Okay.

31:14.289 --> 31:15.331
Take care.

31:25.008 --> 31:29.095
We lost touch after that and didn't see
each other for more than a year.

31:32.891 --> 31:34.309
It was my fault.

31:36.144 --> 31:37.186
What was your fault?

31:37.270 --> 31:40.189
Making assumptions
about someone's feelings.

31:41.566 --> 31:44.319
Overstepping the mark
without having the conviction to do so.

31:44.903 --> 31:48.531
And losing a friend in the process.

31:52.410 --> 31:54.704
But it's water under the bridge now.

31:54.787 --> 31:57.999
I'm happy to just be friends
with her again.

32:00.293 --> 32:01.252
Genuinely.

32:05.173 --> 32:08.176
So, Ms. Lee, you can stop
with your coaching now.

32:11.220 --> 32:12.764
Does that mean I'm fired?

32:13.389 --> 32:15.975
That's a bummer.
I never even got paid for it.

32:23.775 --> 32:24.859
SE-HUN

32:29.656 --> 32:30.865
I'll go take a call.

32:55.932 --> 32:57.141
Who's there?

33:23.835 --> 33:27.422
Doona must be super bored these days.
She wants to hang out almost every day.

33:27.922 --> 33:31.300
It's her first time having friends.
I kind of feel bad for her.

33:32.885 --> 33:34.887
She seems to rely on you a lot.

33:36.139 --> 33:39.267
No, she just likes to tease me.
I'm not much of a person to rely on.

33:40.059 --> 33:42.270
- Should we get these chips?
- Okay.

33:49.152 --> 33:51.487
You underestimate yourself sometimes.

33:53.489 --> 33:54.949
You're quite reliable, you know?

33:57.577 --> 33:59.495
Sorry for the wait. I'll ring you up now.

34:00.955 --> 34:03.041
That's right. It's April Fools' Day.

34:04.333 --> 34:06.669
Has everyone told a lot of lies today?

34:06.753 --> 34:09.297
If not, now's the time.
Lie to me all you want.

34:10.465 --> 34:11.299
Yun-taek.

34:11.924 --> 34:13.051
I love you.

34:14.177 --> 34:15.386
Oh, I love you too.

34:15.470 --> 34:18.306
You jerk, I'm going to kick you
in the face for that!

34:19.307 --> 34:21.059
Someone told me he likes me today.

34:26.397 --> 34:28.149
But I haven't responded yet.

34:28.775 --> 34:29.609
Why not?

34:31.903 --> 34:34.030
Because I'm not sure of my own feelings.

34:38.409 --> 34:39.327
It's weird.

34:40.244 --> 34:42.580
I'll start having feelings for someone,

34:44.040 --> 34:46.542
but as soon as they approach me,
I lose my nerve.

34:48.169 --> 34:50.630
I get afraid that they'll be disappointed…

34:52.632 --> 34:54.383
once they get to know the real me.

35:05.019 --> 35:08.231
What's up with you guys?
I thought we were telling lies.

35:08.731 --> 35:10.274
What's going on?

35:11.067 --> 35:12.735
Why the long face, you guys?

35:13.486 --> 35:15.154
Your acting is out of this world.

35:15.238 --> 35:16.906
Is that what method acting is?

35:17.406 --> 35:18.950
I was totally absorbed just now.

35:19.033 --> 35:20.910
Don't hang out with Doona.
She's rubbing off on you.

35:20.993 --> 35:23.371
That was awesome, Pearl Kim. I like it.

35:25.915 --> 35:27.875
It's Doona's turn next!

35:29.127 --> 35:32.463
What's your lie, Doona?
It's going to be hard to top Jin-ju's.

35:32.547 --> 35:34.423
I think I'm being stalked.

35:36.384 --> 35:37.969
That's an unusual theme for a lie.

35:38.052 --> 35:39.846
I wish it were a lie.

35:43.975 --> 35:45.309
YOU'RE PRETTY

35:46.394 --> 35:47.270
But it's real.

35:47.353 --> 35:48.354
What's this?

35:51.691 --> 35:52.775
You're pretty.

35:54.485 --> 35:55.444
He's here, even now.

36:02.160 --> 36:03.077
Hey, what the hell?

36:03.661 --> 36:05.163
What? What the hell is that?

36:07.373 --> 36:08.207
You creep!

36:14.755 --> 36:16.174
You! Stop right there!

36:16.257 --> 36:17.675
- Hey!
- Won-jun!

36:18.342 --> 36:19.260
Hey!

36:19.343 --> 36:20.970
Get that creep! Get that bastard!

36:21.637 --> 36:23.347
That bastard! That…

36:23.431 --> 36:24.891
Oh, he's turned off.

36:28.102 --> 36:29.145
I've got it!

36:30.188 --> 36:32.398
- All right?
- I've got it! Yes, I'm fine.

36:32.899 --> 36:34.609
- Are you okay?
- It's fine. Thank God.

36:34.692 --> 36:35.610
Get used to it.

36:35.693 --> 36:36.986
He's a heartless jerk.

36:43.159 --> 36:44.368
Hey, let go of me!

36:45.703 --> 36:47.872
I'm not letting you go, you bastard!

36:47.955 --> 36:48.956
Let go!

36:51.542 --> 36:53.044
Hey! You bastard!

36:54.253 --> 36:56.088
- You son of a…
- You son of a bitch!

36:56.172 --> 36:57.423
Are you all right?

36:57.506 --> 36:59.217
You son of a bitch!

36:59.717 --> 37:00.801
Hey, hold him!

37:00.885 --> 37:02.720
You creep. Hold him.

37:02.803 --> 37:03.971
How dare you.

37:23.491 --> 37:24.700
Goddamn it.

37:25.826 --> 37:26.911
- What?
- What?

37:29.080 --> 37:30.414
What a son of a bitch.

37:31.040 --> 37:34.877
I did it out of pure curiosity.
That's all.

37:34.961 --> 37:37.213
I saw her from the store and got excited.

37:37.296 --> 37:39.173
I've been a fan of hers forever, you see.

37:44.720 --> 37:46.305
Let's deal with him ourselves.

37:46.389 --> 37:47.890
What do you have in mind?

37:47.974 --> 37:49.892
He deserves to be beaten
to a goddamn pulp.

37:51.477 --> 37:52.937
I'll just beat him here

37:54.689 --> 37:56.691
until he's at death's door.

37:58.609 --> 37:59.735
A blow to the head?

38:00.736 --> 38:02.405
That might feel satisfying.

38:09.453 --> 38:11.163
- I've always wanted to try it.
- Wait…

38:33.144 --> 38:35.313
Thank God she has common sense, at least.

38:37.732 --> 38:41.277
You. Say one more word, and I'll kill you.

38:41.861 --> 38:42.820
I'm sorry.

38:56.667 --> 38:59.295
Do you really think
it's all right not to call the police?

39:00.504 --> 39:02.798
Doona is dead set against it.

39:02.882 --> 39:04.508
She must have her reasons.

39:06.052 --> 39:09.305
Are you all right?
You look like you're hurt pretty bad--

39:09.388 --> 39:10.431
I'm fine.

39:17.396 --> 39:19.607
I'm going to leave home soon, Won-jun.

39:20.107 --> 39:21.567
That's why I've been working.

39:22.401 --> 39:25.196
Because my dad's against it.

39:25.863 --> 39:27.531
I did wonder what was going on.

39:28.574 --> 39:29.450
Really?

39:58.145 --> 39:58.979
DAD

39:59.063 --> 40:00.898
WHY AREN'T YOU BACK HOME YET, YOU BITCH?

40:00.981 --> 40:03.859
YOU THINK I SENT YOU TO COLLEGE
SO YOU CAN FOOL AROUND WITH MEN?

40:03.943 --> 40:04.944
TEXT ME BACK RIGHT NOW

40:05.027 --> 40:05.861
I'M ON MY WAY

41:26.609 --> 41:28.235
P
YOU'VE GOTTEN BETTER AT LYING

41:28.319 --> 41:30.821
P
STOP CONTACTING ME AND WAIT QUIETLY

42:02.603 --> 42:03.521
You're back.

42:05.356 --> 42:07.399
- Yes.
- You should have woken me up.

42:08.609 --> 42:09.610
I couldn't sleep.

42:10.694 --> 42:12.196
Let me have some beer too.

42:22.665 --> 42:23.874
Why don't you take a seat?

42:42.935 --> 42:47.189
We got his ID, the memory card,
a letter of apology,

42:47.273 --> 42:49.316
and a statement
that he'll never do it again.

42:49.400 --> 42:51.193
We got everything we thought necessary.

42:51.277 --> 42:55.155
We went to his place
and did a factory reset of his computers.

42:55.239 --> 42:57.449
We've made him quit
his convenience store job,

42:57.950 --> 43:00.494
and told his parents and the manager
about what happened.

43:02.997 --> 43:05.958
I'll pass everything on to you,

43:07.501 --> 43:10.504
so you can go to the police
when you feel ready.

43:10.588 --> 43:11.630
Whenever that may be.

43:12.381 --> 43:13.257
I will.

43:16.343 --> 43:17.219
Thank you.

43:22.474 --> 43:24.602
Weren't you scared
dealing with that alone?

43:26.729 --> 43:27.563
Not really.

43:33.527 --> 43:34.528
Doona.

43:36.822 --> 43:40.784
It's okay to be scared.
It's better than getting hurt, you know?

43:44.997 --> 43:47.374
Don't get hurt. Not by anyone.

43:47.458 --> 43:50.252
It was once your job
to be loved by people.

44:06.518 --> 44:08.145
I think I still feel sleepy.

44:09.146 --> 44:10.272
I want to sleep.

44:43.472 --> 44:44.848
I'll hold it for a bit.

44:47.726 --> 44:49.269
Pull away if you don't like it.

47:50.117 --> 47:55.122
Subtitle translation by: Reuben Simpson
